Wiring — every connection

Work with the panel covered, fuses out, and USB unplugged from the ESP32 until 5 V is verified.

Color code: red = +, black = −, yellow = SDA, green = SCL, orange = analog, white = relay IN.

Step 0 — Common ground

Join these negatives together on one ground bus:





Battery −



Solar controller BAT−



XL6009 OUT− and IN−



LM2596 IN− and OUT−



ESP32 GND



Relay GND



All sensor GND



LED lamp −



Inverter − (if used)

If grounds are split, meters and the ESP32 ADC will read nonsense and you can damage boards.



Step 1 — Battery and main fuse





Battery + → 20 A fuse holder → solar controller BAT+.



Battery − → solar controller BAT−.



Leave the fuse out.

LiFePO4 pack already includes a BMS. Do not add XH‑M601 on this pack.





Step 2 — Solar panel to 30 A controller





Panel + → controller PV+.



Panel − → controller PV−.



Optional: insert one dual voltmeter/ammeter in the PV+ line (meter P+ toward panel, P− toward controller) so you can see solar amps.

Controller load terminals (LOAD+/LOAD−): you may power the lamps from here or from the battery via the relay. For ESP32 control, use battery + fuse + relay, not the controller LOAD output.





Step 3 — Wind (Savonius) to battery





Turbine/rectifier + → Schottky anode.



Schottky cathode → XL6009 IN+.



Turbine − → XL6009 IN− (ground).



XL6009 OUT+ (preset 14.4 V) → second Schottky anode.



Schottky cathode → battery + (after the 20 A fuse, same node as BAT+).



XL6009 OUT− → ground bus.

Set 14.4 V on a bench PSU before the turbine is connected.





Step 4 — 5 V electronics rail (LM2596S)





Battery + (after 20 A fuse) → 5 A fuse → LM2596 IN+.



LM2596 IN− → ground.



Adjust LM2596 OUT+ to 5.00 V with a DMM (no ESP32 yet).



LM2596 OUT− → ground.



Optional LM2596-with-display: parallel on the same 5 V to show the rail.

If you also have USB plugged into the ESP32, do not feed 5 V into VIN at the same time.





