Relay NO1 → both 12 V LED bulbs +



Bulbs − → ground

Channel 2 (purifier):





12 V purifier/fan: same pattern as lamps on COM2 / NO2.



AC purifier: relay CH2 switches inverter DC input + (battery + → fuse → COM2 → NO2 → inverter +). Inverter AC out → purifier. Keep AC cables away from ESP32.

Most 5 V relay modules are active LOW: GPIO LOW = ON.





Step 10 — Dual LED volt/amp meters

Meter 1 (solar): shunt in PV+, thin sense wires per the printed silk (usually P+ / P− for current, V+ / V− for voltage).

Meter 2 (battery/load): shunt in the 10 A lamp feed.

These meters are display only. The app uses ACS712 + software.





Step 11 — Waterproof voltage meter (optional)

Red to battery +, black to battery −. It is only a voltmeter.





Step 12 — Breadboards

Use GL‑12 for 5 V / 3.3 V / GND rails and jumper the ESP32 headers. Keep all 12 V on screw terminals, not on the solderless breadboard.





